# kernel-m68k-68000.img -- Linux 6.18.37 for a plain 68000 (no MMU, no FPU)
#
# Runs on qemu-system-m68k -M m68328 from the qemu fork (lordrasmus/qemu,
# branch uclibc-ng): a 68000 with the MC68328's interrupt controller and
# timer, a 16550 at 0xffffe000 on IRQ 2 and 128 MiB of RAM.  Upstream qemu
# has no 68000 machine.  The image is the plain vmlinux (ELF).
#
#   qemu-system-m68k -M m68328 -nographic -kernel kernel-m68k-68000.img \
#     -initrd rootfs.img -append console=ttyS0,115200
#
# The rootfs goes in uncompressed: without an MMU the kernel cannot get a
# large enough contiguous buffer for the xz dictionary.
#
# Build: two separate patches, then kernel-m68k-68000.config.
#
# - kernel-m68k-68000-qemu-board.patch: CONFIG_M68000_QEMU for the m68328
#   machine (setup in arch/m68k/68000/qemu.c, UBOOT-style command line and
#   initrd for the 68000, the initial stack pointer) and qemu68000_defconfig.
# - kernel-m68k-68000-tinfo-flags.patch: upstream 2c6805145e16 ("m68k: Fix
#   task info flags handling for 68000", in v7.1, not in 6.18).  The return
#   to user space read the upper word of thread_info->flags, where no TIF bit
#   lives, so signals were never delivered and preemption never happened on
#   the way out -- a handler never ran, and console output stalled.
#
#   cd linux-6.18.37
#   for p in kernel-m68k-68000-qemu-board.patch \
#            kernel-m68k-68000-tinfo-flags.patch; do patch -p1 < $p; done
#   cp kernel-m68k-68000.config .config
#   make ARCH=m68k CROSS_COMPILE=m68k-openadk-uclinux-uclibc- \
#        olddefconfig vmlinux
#
# The toolchain is the CI's m68k-68000 toolchain (gcc 15.3.0, FLAT).
#
# Known: strtod, strtold, tst-printf-strtod and basic-test fail.  libgcc for
# the 68000 does long double arithmetic in double precision
# (libgcc/config/m68k/fpgnulib.c), so 64-bit mantissas do not survive.
